 "card_notes": [
  {
   "text": "<td style=\"border: 0; padding: 0.55em 0.75em;\"><strong>Context length</strong></td>",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L83"
  },
  {
   "text": "<summary><strong>Chat template</strong></summary>",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L181"
  },
  {
   "text": "LFM3 uses this ChatML format, generated from the checkpoint's [chat template](https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B/blob/main/chat_template.jinja):",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L183"
  },
  {
   "text": "Use `tokenizer.apply_chat_template()` with `add_generation_prompt=True` to format messages automatically.",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L194"
  },
  {
   "text": "Reasoning is enabled by default. You can set `enable_thinking=False` to disable thinking traces, but this behavior can be inconsistent, especially for reasoning-heavy tasks.",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L196"
  },
  {
   "text": "Pass function schemas through `tools=...` to `apply_chat_template()`. The template formats tool definitions and results automatically. Generated calls use XML:",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L205"
  },
  {
   "text": "LFM3 supports deferred tools. Set `defer_loading=True` to keep tool definitions out of the prompt until your harness's search tool returns their names as `tool_reference` parts. The chat template then inserts their definitions into `<additional_tools>`.",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L226"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your harness implements and runs the search. Keep the full `tools` list, including deferred tools, on every request. In the system prompt, tell the model when to search:",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L243"
  },
  {
   "text": "Works with vLLM, SGLang, and LFM3-compatible llama.cpp builds. For llama.cpp, use a GGUF with the current chat template or load it with `--chat-template-file`.",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L247"
  },
  {
   "text": "<p><small>All models were served with vLLM in BF16 at their full context length: 262,144 tokens for LFM3-1.7B, Qwen3.5-4B, and Qwen3.5-9B, and 131,072 tokens for LFM2.5-2.6B, MiniCPM5-2B, and Gemma 4 E4B. Unless listed below, every eval uses temperature 0.6 and top_p 0.95, with no output limit other",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L531"
  },
  {
   "text": "<strong>BFCL V4</strong>: greedy decoding, up to 32,768 output tokens.<br>",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L534"
  },
  {
   "text": "<strong>ToolSandbox</strong>: greedy decoding, up to 1,024 tokens per turn.<br>",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L535"
  },
  {
   "text": "<strong>Claw-Eval</strong>: greedy decoding, 3 trials per task.<br>",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L537"
  },
  {
   "text": "<strong>BrowseComp-Plus</strong>: OpenClaw agent, greedy decoding, up to 8,192 tokens per turn.<br>",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B README.md:L538"
  }
 ],
